      "keyEnv": "TYPESAFE_API_KEY",
      "tools": ["tools/jev-client.js", "tools/jev-arbiter.js", "tools/jev-check.js"],
      "gates": {
        "classifyRoute": 0.6,
        "classifyRouteFlagged": 0.4,
        "seatRoute": 0.6,
        "seatRouteFlagged": 0.4,
        "seatMinMarginToFlip": 0.15,
        "convene": 0.6,
        "netBenefit": 0.6,
        "independentEvidence": 0.6,
        "claimSupported": 0.6,
        "claimContradicted": 0.4
      },
      "policy": "Jev proposes distributions; deterministic code gates. The hosting session stays the driver and runs the tools; Jev reads no files and dispatches nothing. Seat picks come from mix-mode routing.json decisionMatrix2026-09-16 under the margin rule and never name a model whose capacity bucket is exhausted (docs/capacity-state.json). A missing TYPESAFE_API_KEY yields a NOT_RUN result, never a throw; every real call appends a provenance row (request and response sha256, usage, model, timestamp) and never the key. Seats do not call Jev; only the lead runs tools/jev-check.js over seat output, after deterministic pre-checks.",
      "provenance": "jev-decisions.jsonl in the run directory",
      "note": "The principles.arbiter* rows above are unchanged by this block; wiring the Jev classify result into plan-seal and retiring the xai arbiter check in tools/dispatch-matrix.js is a separate, owner-approved step."
    }
  },
